#11901
"White Limestone Room"
"Eight tall, thin and slightly tapering pillars stand upright in the center of

this room, centered around a marble fountain and bench.  The white limestone

surface of the walls cover the poorer quality block and have been polished to

a gentle radiance.  One striking characteristic of this room is the sharply

pointed apex above the western exit, which has been covered with a gold

alloy.  Further to the east and west is complete darkness.

"
""
